## Declared-target verification and C2 structure

[DERIVED] For `lost ∈ {0,1,2,3}`, the declared normalized target is

`forecast_surplus_bits / kappa − lost`,

because the helper accumulates physical surplus only while alive and subtracts one
`kappa` for the failed offset and every later absorbed offset.

[RUN] The row target agreed with a same-call observation of the independent declared
helper to maximum absolute error `3.553e-15`; stored bits equaled forecast surplus minus
persistence penalty exactly. The Q2 valid/survival slots also reconstructed every recorded
